& [UserPurposeCarriedForward]
  + Cantor should resolve input terms toward exact SOP identities records relationships and proof
  + organized concise expression should make speed and accuracy converge without turning correlation into authority
  + the semantic association fabric should remain inspectable and should point back to exact governing material

& [CurrentBoundary]
  + Slice3 exact scanning is completion-proved
  + Slice4A typed relationship paths and association accounts are implemented and focused-verified but full-workspace completion proof is held by host capacity
  + Slice4B lexical behavior is not activated and cannot inherit implementation authority from Slice4A or the P1 verification tool
  + Slice4C compact projection and direct-query equivalence remain later and distinct

& [ObservedLegacyShape]
  + the existing direct query performs trim plus ASCII lowercase and substring containment across expression meaning and aliases
  + it gives lexical matches one fixed additive score only when a term has no exact identity or label match
  + that surface is useful rollback evidence but its additive scalar and substring false positives do not fit the newer PriorityLattice proof model
  + the newer scanner already validates an exact derived catalogue admitted fabric gates channel-local relevance basis points canonical result rebuild and bounded pagination

& [SelectedReadinessDirection]
  + compile a deterministic lexical token-posting index from admitted preferred expressions aliases and exact meaning text
  + bind the tokenizer profile index postings surface identity and evidence references inside the disposable derived catalogue proof
  + retrieve postings for lexical-eligible query terms instead of scanning every unit on every query
  + attach a typed lexical match account to each lexical contribution so original terms normalized tokens matched tokens surface kinds and evidence remain machine-readable
  + compute relevance basis points only as exact unique-token coverage under one declared formula
  + use no stop-word list stemming synonym inference fuzzy edit distance n-grams embeddings learned weights or subject-text inference in P0
  + gather lexical proposals only for terms that produced no exact identity or exact-label proposal under enabled earlier channels
  + gate every proposed exact SemanticAddress through the same lifecycle authority purpose context and boundary operator before ranking

& [BudgetNeed]
  + add an exact maximum_lexical_postings budget rather than borrowing relation path record elapsed or byte meanings
  + fail before partial lexical output when the complete selected posting set exceeds that budget because a cursor that only paginates finalized candidates cannot resume incomplete discovery honestly
  + aggregate all admitted postings within budget then rank and truncate new lower-tier candidates after complete lexical scoring
  + existing exact and higher-tier candidates retain capacity precedence

& [TokenizerQuestion]
  + a tokenizer must declare case Unicode punctuation token-order and duplicate semantics rather than rely on an unspecified language-model interpretation
  + Unicode-aware standard-library classification may vary with the compiled toolchain Unicode tables and therefore needs a versioned lexical profile and compiler identity
  + preserve original query and surface text outside tokens and perform no confusable folding or silent Unicode normalization

& [ScoringQuestion]
  + one candidate may match across several query terms and several surfaces
  + aggregate unique query-token coverage across lexical-eligible terms so multi-term coherence is visible
  + use floor of matched unique query tokens times ten-thousand divided by total unique query tokens
  + do not add field prestige probability truth confidence risk authority or permission into that number
  + equal winning lexical coverage remains explicit ambiguity

& [ProofNeed]
  + prove index equality with a fresh admitted-fabric rebuild and mutation refusal for tokenizer profile token posting surface meaning reference unit package and roots
  + prove no substring false positives token duplication score inflation exact-tier displacement or cross-channel arithmetic
  + prove complete-posting budget refusal deterministic candidate order exact gate reuse and byte-identical replay
  + compare legacy direct-query exact overlap later under Slice4C without requiring lexical score equivalence

& [ReadinessDisposition]
  + preserve and review this design now
  + do not phase-lock implement test or claim Slice4B until Slice4A has its reserved full completion proof
  + no provider model persistence remote hidden-state effect FPGA OneDrive EVO-X2 or Minecraft behavior
